userStories.description:
Set up the design system and top-level shell layout. Rorcha uses a dark-first monochrome palette: near-black bg (#0f0f11), zinc-800 panels, zinc-700 borders, white text, indigo-500 accent. No external component library — build primitives inline using Tailwind.

Design tokens in ~/rorcha/src/styles/tokens.css:
```css
:root {
  --bg: #0f0f11;
  --panel: #1c1c21;
  --border: #3f3f46;
  --text: #fafafa;
  --text-muted: #a1a1aa;
  --accent: #6366f1;
  --accent-hover: #818cf8;
  --success: #22c55e;
  --warning: #f59e0b;
  --error: #ef4444;
}
```

Import tokens.css in main.tsx. Update tailwind.config.ts to use CSS variables:
```typescript
theme: { extend: { colors: {
  bg: 'var(--bg)', panel: 'var(--panel)', border: 'var(--border)',
  accent: 'var(--accent)', muted: 'var(--text-muted)',
}}}
```

Shell component ~/rorcha/src/components/Shell.tsx:
- Top nav: 48px, bg-panel, border-b border-border
  - Left: 'rorcha' wordmark (font-mono, text-accent, font-bold)
  - Right: workspace selector dropdown (populated from GET /api/workspaces) + gear icon
- Main content: flex row, h-[calc(100vh-48px)]
  - Left sidebar: 56px wide, icon-only nav (see U-002)
  - Content area: flex-1, the active panel renders here

Workspace selector:
- Fetches GET /api/workspaces on mount
- Stores selected workspaceId in React context (WorkspaceContext)
- Falls back to first workspace if none selected
- 'Add Workspace' option at bottom of dropdown → opens AddWorkspaceModal (stub for now)

All data fetching uses a shared authFetch wrapper:
```typescript
export async function apiFetch<T>(path: string, opts?: RequestInit): Promise<T> {
  const base = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3030';
  const res = await fetch(`${base}${path}`, opts);
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`${res.status} ${await res.text()}`);
  return res.json() as Promise<T>;
}
```

File: ~/rorcha/src/contexts/WorkspaceContext.tsx
- WorkspaceProvider wraps App, provides { workspaceId, setWorkspaceId, workspaces }

The Direction Stack panel lets users view and edit L1/L2/L3 direction layers for the active workspace. Real-time preview merges all layers into the synthesized output.

File: ~/rorcha/src/panels/DirectionStackPanel.tsx

Layout: 3 columns at equal width
- Column 1: Layer editor tabs (L1, L2, L3)
  - Tab buttons at top: L1 Global Brain | L2 Domain Profile | L3 Project Brief
  - Content: <textarea> (full height, mono font, bg-bg, border border-border, resize-none)
  - Each layer loads from GET /api/direction-stack?workspaceId=&layer={1|2|3}
  - Save button (POST /api/direction-stack) — debounced 500ms auto-save with visual indicator
  - Unsaved indicator: dim dot next to layer tab when content modified but not yet saved

- Column 2: L4 Spec Brief + L5 Story Annotations (ephemeral, no save)
  - Two stacked textareas, labeled 'Spec Brief (L4)' and 'Story Annotations (L5)'
  - These are only used for preview (wired to synthesis call below)
  - Placeholder text explains the layer purpose

- Column 3: Synthesized preview (read-only)
  - Header: 'Synthesized Output' + character count
  - Content: scrollable pre block, bg-bg, font-mono, text-sm, text-text
  - Auto-updates when any layer changes (debounced 300ms)
  - Fetches from POST /api/direction-stack/synthesize with { workspaceId, l4SpecBrief, l5Annotations }
  - Loading state: text-muted 'Synthesizing...' with spin animation
  - Copy button: copies full synthesized text to clipboard

Shared custom hook: useDirectionLayer(workspaceId: string, layer: 1|2|3)
```typescript
export function useDirectionLayer(workspaceId: string, layer: 1|2|3) {
  const [content, setContent] = useState('');
  const [isSaving, setIsSaving] = useState(false);
  const [isDirty, setIsDirty] = useState(false);
  // load on mount, auto-save on change (debounced)
  return { content, setContent, isSaving, isDirty };
}
```
